    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (only `AcceptanceTest` exists; both of its tests pass).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe membership tier is a derived, read-only field on the owner response, so I implemented it alongside the other derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber`) rather than persisting it:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `membershipTier` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is generated from this spec at build time).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression to `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0\n       && owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank() ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\"\n   ```\n\nThis returns `SILVER` when `namesakeCount` is 0 **and** an email is present, and `BRONZE` otherwise \u2014 matching the spec and both acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`).",
